# Role
You are writing the pure derivation of the companion's appearance from what
the user has redeemed. No I/O, no Prisma: same discipline as points.ts.

The companion's look is **never stored as its own state** — it is always
derived from redemptions, so the avatar cannot drift out of sync with what
the user actually paid for.

# Requirements
Write two functions in `src/lib/look.ts`.

**`summarizeOwned(redemptions: RedeemedItem[]): OwnedRewardSummary[]`**
- Groups redemptions per reward item, counting duplicates.
- Keeps the **earliest** redemption date per item — that's the "when did I
  earn this" the collection displays.
- Sorted by that first-earned date, so the collection reads as a timeline.

**`buildLook(redemptions: RedeemedItem[]): Look`**
- Accessories are worn **oldest first** and **deduped by emoji**: redeeming
  the same hat twice must not stack two hats on the sprite.
- Cap worn accessories at 4 so a heavy spender doesn't bury the companion
  under emoji. Everything still appears in the collection.
- The **most recently redeemed** theme wins, so buying a new theme visibly
  replaces the old backdrop instead of appearing to do nothing.
- Ignore a theme whose `themeKey` isn't one of `meadow | dusk | sunrise` —
  render no backdrop rather than a broken one.
- `skip-token` items are **not** worn: they're inventory, not an outfit.
- Do not mutate the input array (sort a copy).

# Interface
```ts
interface RedeemedItem {
  rewardItemId: string;
  kind: string;          // "accessory" | "theme" | "skip-token"
  emoji: string;
  themeKey: string | null;
  redeemedAt: Date;
}

interface OwnedRewardSummary {
  rewardItemId: string;
  count: number;
  firstRedeemedAt: string; // ISO
}

interface Look {
  accessories: string[];
  themeEmoji?: string;
  themeKey?: "meadow" | "dusk" | "sunrise";
}
```

# Dependencies
None — this module must stay pure.

# Acceptance criteria (see tests/look.test.ts)
- No redemptions -> `{ accessories: [] }`.
- Accessories appear oldest-first regardless of input order.
- The same accessory redeemed twice appears once.
- Six accessories yield exactly 4 worn.
- With two themes redeemed, the later one's `themeKey` and `themeEmoji` win.
- An unrecognized `themeKey` leaves `themeKey` undefined.
- A `skip-token` is never worn.
- The input array's order is unchanged after the call.
- `summarizeOwned` counts duplicates, keeps the earliest date, and orders by
  first-earned.
